Diagnostic-only SPSS offline seal for the secure-heap kexec experiment.

Default off. This does not reclaim memory by itself and is not the final Android
kexec fix. Preserve the existing vendor ABI and use only after freezing userspace
inside normal kexec. The test build also uses the separately validated GIC handoff.
Apply to the kernel tree after the base kexec KABI patch; no source checkout is
modified by storing this patch.

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/Kconfig
@@ -14,6 +14,18 @@
 
 if REMOTEPROC
 
+config REMOTEPROC_KEXEC_OFFLINE_GATE
+	bool "One-shot offline remoteproc seal for kexec diagnostics"
+	depends on ARM64 && KEXEC_CORE && FREEZER && OF
+	default n
+	help
+	  Permit a kexec-only caller, after freezing userspace, to permanently
+	  block Linux boot, attach and recovery of one already offline remote
+	  processor. The remoteproc must remain unused with automatic boot off
+	  and recovery disabled. No remote processor is stopped by this option.
+	  A successful seal cannot be undone before reset. This is intended for
+	  controlled kexec diagnostics, not normal remoteproc lifecycle control.
+
 config REMOTEPROC_CDEV
 	bool "Remoteproc character device interface"
 	help
